cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "CollisionRiskAlgo: An ADS-B Algorithm for Quantifying Proximity Encounters and Traffic Exposure Around Go-Arounds"
abstract: >-
  CollisionRiskAlgo detects go-arounds in ADS-B surveillance data and
  quantifies proximity risk in the terminal airspace around them. Each
  second, every aircraft pair within 10 nautical miles of the airport is
  evaluated against three proximity thresholds, from standard radar
  separation (3 NM, 1,000 ft) to a near mid-air collision volume, using
  observed positions and 120-second straight-line projections. Encounter
  counts and traffic exposure (aircraft-pair time) in the ten minutes
  before and after each go-around are compared with the same change around
  full-stop landings at matching times of day, with day-block bootstrap
  confidence intervals, a traffic-adjusted baseline, placebo, pre-trend,
  robustness and sensitivity checks.
authors:
